OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Up to 50 million people all over the
OL,6, world are said to have taken part in
OL,7, this afternoon's global fun run being
OL,8, organised by Sport Aid.
OL,10,FAt least 120 countries joined the race
OL,11,Fwhich was televised to a potential
OL,12,Fworld audience of 1.5 billion.
OL,14,FThe main event in Britain was in
OL,15,FLondon's Hyde Park, where 100,000
OL,16,Fpeople ran the six-mile course.
OL,17,F
OL,18,FThe first Sport Aid Race Against Time
OL,19,Fwas in 1986; 20 million people ran and
OL,20,F#24 million was raised for charity.
OL,23,D]CFrom 11-09-88   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
